17:01.000 --> 17:07.000
So what time frame was Jessie of Balranald? When did this happen, with Jessie of Balranald?

17:08.000 --> 17:15.000
Oh, it must have been before 1849 I would say. I couldn’t say the date at all.

17:15.000 --> 17:19.000
Och that’s alright, just kind of the time frame, 1800s. 

17:19.000 --> 17:29.000
1800s, oh yes I’m sure. But Jessie you know was in love with this boy from Skye. 

17:30.000 --> 17:38.000
And he was in Skye, and he was a… when they were in Skye, 

17:38.000 --> 17:40.000
when the MacDonald’s of Balranald were in Skye. 

17:40.000 --> 17:45.000
And he was the factor at that time, in Skye. 

17:45.000 --> 17:48.000
And he fell in love with Jessie.

17:48.000 --> 17:58.000
But this man came to Uist, Patrick Cooper, and he fell in love, 

17:58.000 --> 18:01.000
she was a lovely woman, and he fell in love with her. 

18:01.000 --> 18:04.000
And this was the man, he was the factor, 

18:05.000 --> 18:09.000
they made him a factor so that he would marry Jessie. 

18:10.000 --> 18:17.000
But this man came from Skye, and they were corresponding all the time. 

18:17.000 --> 18:21.000
She would rather have this Skyeman than Patrick Cooper. 

18:21.000 --> 18:34.000
And they went to, they went, they were corresponding anyway, and he said…

18:34.000 --> 18:38.000
she phoned him, eh not phoned him but wrote to him or… 

18:38.000 --> 18:42.000
she got a message to him anyway that they were making preparations 

18:42.000 --> 18:46.000
for her marriage to Patrick Cooper, and that she didn’t like this 

18:46.000 --> 18:53.000
and they made the, oh a big do you know with dancing and music and drink and everything. 

18:54.000 --> 18:59.000
But that very night he was coming from Skye with a boat, 

19:00.000 --> 19:06.000
and she complained of a sore head and went to bed early. 

19:07.000 --> 19:15.000
And there was somebody who gave him the information of the bedroom she was in 

19:15.000 --> 19:18.000
and all and he got a ladder and took her out 

19:18.000 --> 19:23.000
and they went down to the boat, and took her away. 

19:23.000 --> 19:27.000
But a gale had blown by this time 

19:27.000 --> 19:31.000
and they had to land in Rhodel in Harris,

19:31.000 --> 19:34.000
and who was in Rhodel at that time but her uncle! 

19:35.000 --> 19:44.000
And they knew, well, they took her in and she had to sleep that night, 

19:44.000 --> 19:48.000
she was a prisoner there that night. But he said to her:

19:48.000 --> 19:51.000
“Before the sun sets tomorrow, I’ll be back again.”

19:51.000 --> 20:01.000
And they came back with a boat and eight or ten strong men with him, 

20:02.000 --> 20:11.000
and he managed to know, Jessie had given one of the maids word to meet him. 

20:11.000 --> 20:15.000
And she went out, the maid, and told him the bedroom 

20:15.000 --> 20:20.000
and all and then they didn’t know what to do, 

20:20.000 --> 20:27.000
but they took the mast out of the boat and just rammed the big door in, 

20:28.000 --> 20:32.000
and then the trouble started. 

20:33.000 --> 20:39.000
Guns and everything were produced and every man who was knocked down, 

20:39.000 --> 20:43.000
everyone in the hotel was knocked down and tied, 

20:43.000 --> 20:46.000
tied there and they took her away again. 

20:46.000 --> 20:52.000
And they got married in Glasgow, and went away to Astràilia. 

20:52.000 --> 20:57.000
And some folk were telling that they met their grandchildren in Astràilia.

20:59.000 --> 21:03.000
Seadh. Sin agad e.

21:04.000 --> 21:07.000
Aye... can you record that to me?

21:07.000 --> 21:10.000
Aye, play it back?

21:09.000 --> 21:10.000
Aye.

21:10.000 --> 21:11.000
[BREAK IN TAPE]

21:11.000 --> 21:14.000
Duine fhoghlamaichte a bh’ ann am MacCodrum na anns an linn anns an robh e beò. 

21:14.000 --> 21:19.000
Chaidh iad uair dhan Eilean Sgitheanach agus dh’fhaighnich iad... 

21:19.000 --> 21:23.000
chaidh iad a shuidhe ann a shin agus dh’fhaighnich iad, am boireannach dha, 

21:23.000 --> 21:30.000
cò as a [XX] imire? Thog esan a ghàirdeannan. Thuirt MacCodrum:

